    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` with 2 tests) passes and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required owner responses to carry `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`. I implemented it following the repo's existing convention for derived response fields (`bulkSignupWarning`, `Locality`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setContactPreference`.\n2. **`ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny cohesive helper mirroring `BulkSignupWarning`: `of(owner)` returns `\"EMAIL\"` when `owner.getEmail() != null`, else `\"PHONE\"` (using the same \"email present\" definition already used by `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`).\n3. **`RespondWithOwner`** / **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 one line each calling the helper, placed exactly where `bulkSignupWarning` is set (GET and POST responders, matching existing placement).\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: the decision logic lives in a new class with zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), and each edited responder stays CC 1 with a single changed line \u2014 no growth of the large `OwnerMapper` class.",
